{Out before ...e6, as always in the Advance. [%tags bishop-placement light-squares]} 4. d4
{White completes the Advance setup. [%weight 7]} 4... e6
{Build the wall behind the bishop. [%plan This is chapter 2 after 4.Nf3. Expect 5.Be2 and play ...c5 against the base of the chain.] [%line 2.Nf3 into the Advance]}
) ( 3. Nc3 {The Two Knights by the other order. [%weight 5]} 3... Bg4
{The same answer as ever: the bishop comes out and heads for f3. [%tags vs-two-knights bishop-placement] [%plan Play ...Bxf3 when asked, then ...Nf6 and ...e6. This is the Two Knights position from earlier in this chapter.] [%line 2.Nf3 and 3.Nc3]}
) ( 3. d3 {White gives up on the centre entirely. [%weight 3]} 3... dxe4
{Take. White has to recapture with a pawn and the queens come off. [%tags tactics]}
4. dxe4
{Forced, and now the d-file is open with the queens facing each other. [%weight 9]}
4... Qxd1+
